# Generated from: specs/314-repair-obsolete-steering-manifests-during-project-upgrades/requirements.md
Feature: Repair obsolete steering manifests during project upgrades
  Current-layout projects with obsolete byteBound snippet fields were rejected by
  strict runtime loading, while upgrade detection incorrectly reported no repair.
  The explicit upgrade boundary now proposes a digest-bound manifest-only repair
  without weakening ordinary runtime validation.

  # --- Bug Is Fixed ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Upgrade detects an obsolete current-layout manifest without mutation
    Given a project has a current-layout steering manifest with a byteBound snippet field and no legacy steering Markdown
    When project-upgrade detection runs
    Then one actionable managed steering-runtime repair is reported
    And every project file remains byte-for-byte unchanged

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Approved repair removes only byteBound
    Given an unchanged approved repair for a current-layout manifest with registered snippets, extensions, and validations
    When project upgrade applies the repair
    Then byteBound is absent from every snippet record
    And every other registration and project-owned file is preserved
    And repeating detection reports no steering-runtime repair

  # --- Related Behavior Still Works ---

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Prompt fragments load after the approved repair
    Given the obsolete current-layout manifest has been repaired through project upgrade
    When project prompt fragments are loaded for sdlc-write-spec
    Then loading succeeds without project_runtime_invalid or steering_manifest_unknown_key

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: README requires project upgrade after installation changes
    Given a user installs or updates nmg-sdlc
    When the user reads the installation guidance
    Then the user is directed to run sdlc-upgrade-project after every install or update
    And applicable approved migrations must be completed before other SDLC workflows

  # --- Edge Cases ---

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Unknown fields and stale evidence remain fail closed
    Given a repair input contains byteBound plus another unknown snippet field or its approved source digest has changed
    When upgrade detection or apply validates the input
    Then no partial live mutation occurs
    And validation fails with steering_manifest_unknown_key or steering_plan_stale as applicable
    And ordinary runtime loading remains strict
